title: 'statement gossip: route v2 DHT propagation through the per-peer outbox'

doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    On nodes running the v2 DHT statement path, statements the orchestrator targets at a peer
    now go through the same per-peer outbox as v1 propagation: one chunk in flight per peer,
    the shared in-flight byte budget, a bounded queue and a retry after a failed store fetch.
    The orchestrator has already chosen the peer, so its affinity filter and sync watermark are
    not applied to them, and a scheduled initial sync no longer clears the outbox on that path.
    A queued statement that left the store or expired before its chunk went out, or was still
    queued when the peer disconnected, is counted in `undelivered_statements` under
    `missing_from_store` or `disconnected`. Nodes without the v2 DHT path enabled are unaffected.

crates:
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: patch
